-- Sell a Million Sushi (place 125866884667103) - Matcha LuauVM
-- Version: 2.5.0 -- v2.4.1 pickup + overlay, plus market-gated auto deposit
--
-- WHAT THIS ADDS: when the live fish-market multiplier reaches the slider value, teleport
-- ONTO Plot.Sell.DepositButton.Button ONCE, fire the touch, return, and measure whether
-- CurrentCount actually dropped. Latch until the value falls below the threshold again.
--
-- CONFIRMED (probed 2026-11-02):
--   Market value is readable text on Plot.Restaurant.Interior.KitchenBoard.MarketBoard:
--       Price = "Fish Value: 1.4x"   -> parse (%d+%.?%d*)x
--       Next  = "Updating in 9s"
--   Deposit target: Workspace.Plots.<plot>.Sell.DepositButton.Button
--     (Model -> Part "Button" -> TouchTransmitter "TouchInterest")
--   CurrentCount = LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("CurrentCount") (number)
--   NetWorth     = LocalPlayer:GetAttribute("NetWorth") (STRING like "$2.6M")
--   Drawing.new supports Text/Square/Line/Circle/Quad/Triangle/Image
--
-- UNVERIFIED, and why this build MEASURES instead of claiming:
--   firetouchinterest on Sell.CollectButton did nothing in two earlier tests, and every
--   button's server script returns "Invalid bytecodes" so we cannot read what it checks.
--   v2.5.0 therefore reports `lastDeposit=` as either "took N fish" (CurrentCount fell)
--   or "no change". Do not trust a deposit that the report did not see.

